# 2026-08-20 fix: these data/*.json files are byte-identical copies of
# their dashboard/*.json counterparts (scraper/fetch.py's
# write_json_outputs/write_category_json write both on every run).
# Nothing reads them back as state - fetch.py always regenerates them
# fresh each run, and any previous-run state it needs (first-seen
# dates, carry-forward) is read from dashboard/*.json instead. Keeping
# a second committed copy of the same ~100MB+ dataset roughly doubled
# the size of every Summit commit for no benefit. They stay on disk
# each run for any same-run tooling that wants them (e.g. the CSV
# export step) - they just stop being committed. If you added a new
# reader that expects one of these to exist in a *fresh checkout*
# (not just the current run), untrack it from this list first.
data/records.json
data/records.enriched.json
data/hot_stack.json
data/sheriff_sales.json
data/probate.json
data/code_violations.json
data/vacant_homes.json
